From f1c7ccd3478a984da78e43018f0a625b7e45723d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 17:06:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [AGS] gfxfilter_sdl_renderer: collapse to the one filter this
 driver uses

Follows 0029: gfxfilter_sdl_renderer.h/.cpp's bare #include <SDL_render.h>
was the second (and, after this patch, last) file in the tree keeping a
bare SDL2-style include -- confirmed the real remaining blocker by a
full cmake --build build/ags -j$(nproc) -- -k pass after 0030, which
showed exactly this family (gfxfilter_sdl_renderer.h/.cpp,
gfxfilter_aa_sdl_renderer.h/.cpp, and gfxdriverfactory.cpp as a pure
downstream consumer) as the only remaining Engine-side blocker.

SDLRendererGfxFilter::GetScaleMode()/InitSDLHint() picked an
SDL_Renderer texture scale mode and an SDL_HINT_RENDER_SCALE_QUALITY
hint -- both meaningless once patch 0029's present step stopped using
SDL_Renderer at all and started calling SDL_BlitSurfaceScaled() with a
hardcoded SDL_SCALEMODE_NEAREST directly; nothing in the driver has
called either method since 0029 landed. SDLRendererAAGfxFilter (the
second, "Linear", filter) inherited the same dead GetScaleMode()
override and was equally inert. Rather than just fix the includes and
rename SDL_ScaleModeNearest/Linear to their SDL3 spellings (confirmed
via a scratch stub that this alone doesn't even compile --
SDL_HINT_RENDER_SCALE_QUALITY does not exist in SDL3 at all, per
SDL_oldnames.h), collapsed to the one filter the v0.1 profile actually
offers (PLAN.md's review-decision section: "no scaling, no filtering"),
matching PATCH-SEQUENCE.md's own 0029 row. gfxfilter_aa_sdl_renderer.h/.cpp
are deleted outright (confirmed via a tree-wide grep: referenced nowhere
outside ali3dsw.cpp and their own files) and removed from
Engine/CMakeLists.txt's file list; GetFilterCount()/GetFilterInfo()/
CreateFilter() in ali3dsw.cpp updated to match. The one remaining
filter keeps its existing "StdScale" ID unchanged (not renamed to
something like "None") since a config file could persist this ID and
there is no reason to break that compatibility for a rename with no
behavioral consequence.

Verified beyond the usual scratch-stub isolation this time: a full
cmake --build build/ags -j$(nproc) -- -k pass compiled ali3dsw.cpp.obj
and gfxfilter_sdl_renderer.cpp.obj against the real, unstubbed headers
together with zero errors -- the first time these files have compiled
for real as a set, not just individually against a throwaway stub.
That same full-build pass surfaced a separate, unrelated finding in
Common/ (five files with real compile errors, none previously ever
attempted -- see the next patches).
